## Podcasts
- [Getting Started with Slack Apps and Slack AI](https://www.heroku.com/codeish-podcasts/getting-started-with-slack-apps-and-slack-ai/): \<p\>Slack can be so much more than a way to chat with your colleagues\. In this episode of Code\[ish\], we’re joined by Maria José Hernández to find out how Slack Apps and Slack AI can elevate the app into an organization\-wide, personalized work OS\.\</p\>
- [Kubernetes World: Finding Your Path in the Cloud Native Ecosystem](https://www.heroku.com/codeish-podcasts/kubernetes-finding-your-path-in-the-cloud-native-ecosystem/): Bart Farrell from KubeFM and LearnKube joins Julian and Yadin to discuss Kubernetes World: Finding Your Path in the Cloud Native Ecosystem, a new free ebook and career guide that helps new community members navigate the complex Kubernetes landscape\. From the importance of a welcoming community to a behind\-the\-scenes look at how the ebook was created, this episode will interest all cloud\-native professionals\.
- [Heroku in the Wild: Saving Lives with Nonprofit Watch Duty](https://www.heroku.com/codeish-podcasts/saving-lives-with-nonprofit-watch-duty/): During the Los Angeles wildfires in 2025, more than 10 million people relied on Watch Duty for potentially life\-saving information\. On this episode of Code\[ish\], its Cofounder and CTO Dave Merrick talks Julián Duque through how the application works and the technologies like Heroku that make it possible\.
- [Special Episode: Active for Good](https://www.heroku.com/codeish-podcasts/special-episode-active-for-good/): \<p\>During a time of uncertainty, it can be helpful to remember that opportunities to provide help are all around us\. One such group with a unique approach to philanthropy is Active for Good\. Active for Good is an app which tracks the number of calories you burn, and in exchange for that movement, donates a meal packet to malnourished children\. Troy Hickerson and Luke Mysse join Charlie Gleason to talk about their work on Active for Good, sharing their personal stories of how they got involved as well as providing inspiration on what "good tech" can look like\.\</p\>
- [Special Episode: Scaling Businesses During a Pandemic](https://www.heroku.com/codeish-podcasts/special-episode-scaling-businesses-during-a-pandemic/): \<p\>The COVID pandemic has forever changed the way businesses operate; many shops have had to shut down, due to the lack of foot traffic\. For the others who were fortunate enough to shift online, questions around distribution and logistics increased as visitor traffic spiked\. Ryan Townsend, the CTO of SHIFT Commerce, discusses the ways in which his PaaS has helped online retailers manage higher order volumes efficiently\.\</p\>

